  "worked_solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. This is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(\\sqrt{t}-3)\\,i+t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{t}-3,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2t\\,i+(\\sqrt{t}-3)^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+(t-6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{\u2032}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}-3)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\u2032}(t) & =(2t\\,i+(t-6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =2t\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+t-6\\sqrt{t}+9 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{t}+t-6\\sqrt{t}+9 \\\\  & =t-5\\sqrt{t}+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-5\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
